Ladybird’s UI process now writes to the system clipboard, for a
renderer, only text/plain, text/html, and image/png data, which are
the only formats a page’s own clipboard writes produce.

In Chromium, the renderer writes to the clipboard only through the
typed methods of ClipboardHostImpl, in content/browser/renderer_host/
clipboard_host_impl.cc (WriteText(), WriteHtml(), WriteImage(), and
so on), so it never names a native clipboard format. And the one that
takes a URL, WriteBookmark(), drops a file: URL outright.

This comparison comes from reading Chromium’s source.
